SSB microphone gain help

1. Connect a suitable antenna or dummy load. Set RF power low and check that the frequency is clear.
2. Hold the microphone as you normally would when transmitting.
3. Press Space, then y to start ALC monitoring.
4. Hold PTT and say your callsign in your normal on-air voice.
5. Release PTT. YAC reports the peak ALC in speech or braille.
6. With PTT released, press comma to decrease mic gain or full stop to increase it.
7. Repeat steps 4 to 6 until the ALC indication meets the guidance in your radio manual.

q) Return to Settings and keep the mic gain.

